---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy – Transparent Data & Cookies Notice"
  description={`How ${siteConfig.name} handles preferences, local storage, advertising cookies, and browser permissions.`}
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plain-Language Policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
      Last updated: September 2026. At {siteConfig.name}, we believe in transparent, minimalist data practices.
      We do not require user accounts, passwords, or personal profiles. All core calculations and timekeeping functions
      execute 100% locally within your web browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Local Storage and Preferences</h2>
    <p>
      Your user preferences—including saved timer presets, active alarm schedules, preferred world clock cities,
      time zone converter pairings, and light/dark theme selection—are stored exclusively in your browser's
      <code>localStorage</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Running countdown timers store an end-timestamp in <code>sessionStorage</code> so that refreshing the tab
      or reopening a closed tab restores your countdown without losing elapsed time. None of this data is ever
      transmitted to or stored on our servers.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Advertising & Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      To help support the ongoing hosting and development of our free instruments, {siteConfig.name} works with
      third-party advertising partners, including <strong>Google AdSense</strong>.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website
        or other websites on the Internet.
      </li>
      <li>
        Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve personalized or non-personalized ads
        based on your visits to our site and other sites across the web.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your Choices & Opt-Out:</strong> You may opt out of personalized advertising at any time by visiting
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.
        Alternatively, you can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aboutads.info</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Server Logs & Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      When you load pages on {siteConfig.name}, our static hosting provider automatically receives standard HTTP
      request metadata, such as your IP address, browser user-agent, and the requested page URL. This technical data
      is used solely for content delivery, DDOS mitigation, and server security.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser Permissions (Notifications & Wake Lock)</h2>
    <p>
      We will only request browser permissions when you explicitly click a corresponding control:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Notifications:</strong> Used solely to alert you when an alarm or timer completes. You can revoke
        notification privileges at any time in your browser settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Screen Wake Lock:</strong> Used solely when you enable the "Keep screen awake" toggle on the clock or timer,
        preventing your display from dimming during study or cooking sessions.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to Delete Your Data</h2>
    <p>
      Because your data is saved only in your device's browser, you have complete control. You can delete individual
      alarms or saved cities directly inside the app, or clear your browser's cookies and site data for
      <code>{siteConfig.name}</code> to permanently wipe all stored settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about our privacy practices, please contact us at
      <a href="mailto:contact@clockgarden.com">contact@clockgarden.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
